   "text": {
    "L1": "A Friend’s Prayer is a prayer to be a good friend, not a request for gifts.",
    "L2": "The opening word is “May”. It asks for something good for the friendship.",
    "L3": "The speaker wants to give her very best and help her friends’ wishes come true.",
    "L4": "She wants to see with her heart and love her friends the way they are.",
    "L5": "So she will not judge friends from afar. She will accept them instead.",
    "L6": "The poem has rhyming couplets, such as “share” and “care”.",
    "L7": "Remember: after “May”, use the plain verb, as in “May my friend get well”.",
    "L8": "Now choose the idea that best states what the poem is about."
   },
